<%# The orientation strip: how much work is waiting, how much is running, how much
    has stalled on a person, and how the queue splits by direction. Backlog counts
    are the WHOLE queue rather than the filtered slice — a filter narrows what you
    are reading, it does not change how much work there is. %>
<div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-8 gap-2 mb-4">
  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg px-3 py-2">
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Queued</div>
    <div class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 tabular-nums"><%= number_with_delimiter(counts[:queued]) %></div>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg px-3 py-2">
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">In flight</div>
    <div class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 tabular-nums"><%= number_with_delimiter(counts[:in_flight]) %></div>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg px-3 py-2">
    <%# Beside "In flight" rather than folded into it: these are the items that
        have stopped and are waiting on a person, and a queue that is not draining
        is usually this number rather than the one to its left. %>
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Parked on a person</div>
    <div class="text-xl font-bold text-amber-700 tabular-nums"><%= number_with_delimiter(counts[:parked]) %></div>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg px-3 py-2">
    <%# The items the fleet started and dropped. It reads as zero on a healthy
        deployment, because the hourly sweep puts back everything whose session
        left nothing behind — so anything here is something the sweep looked at
        and deliberately left, and the rows say which. %>
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Stranded</div>
    <div class="text-xl font-bold text-rose-700 tabular-nums"><%= number_with_delimiter(counts[:stranded]) %></div>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg px-3 py-2">
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Queued convergent</div>
    <div class="text-xl font-bold text-emerald-700 tabular-nums"><%= number_with_delimiter(queued_by_direction[Issues::Direction::CONVERGENT]) %></div>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg px-3 py-2">
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Queued divergent</div>
    <div class="text-xl font-bold text-violet-700 tabular-nums"><%= number_with_delimiter(queued_by_direction[Issues::Direction::DIVERGENT]) %></div>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg px-3 py-2">
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Open on GitHub</div>
    <div class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 tabular-nums"><%= number_with_delimiter(counts[:github_open]) %></div>
  </div>
  <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg px-3 py-2">
    <%# The pile the issue gate has not reached. It is the number that says
        whether the queue is a picture of the work or a corner of it. %>
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Open &amp; unrated</div>
    <div class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-700 tabular-nums"><%= number_with_delimiter(github_by_direction[Issues::Direction::UNRATED]) %></div>
  </div>
</div>
